ntime\",\"offset\":2410}],\"excerpt\":\"…activated; the task can therefore begin execution immediately upon assignment. In the AOT mode, the runtime pre-enqueues the task to a worker before its predecessor event is activated. The worker cannot execute the task until the dependent event is fully activated, and thus waits locally for the dependency to be satisfied.\\nJIT and AOT approaches involve complementary advantages. On the one hand,…\"},{\"filename\":\"paper_secs/secs_multimodal_kernel/Mirage Persistent Kernel A Compiler and Runtime for Mega-Kernelizing Tensor Programs/span-idpage-6-0span5.1-Event-Driven-Execution.md\",\"basename\":\"span-idpage-6-0span5.1-Event-Driven-Execution\",\"score\":6199.1509786299885,\"foundWords\":[\"mirage\",\"mega-kernelizing\",\"persistent\",\"kernel\",\"kernelizing\",\"compiler\",\"runtime\",\"mega\"],\"matches\":[{\"match\":\"runtime\",\"offset\":1001}],\"excerpt\":\"…r of times. When an event is activated, it is enqueued into a scheduler's event queue, allowing the runtime to continue propagating execution through the *t*Graph. In this way, events serve as the mechanism for driving task execution, enabling fine-grained, asynchronous execution.\"},{\"filename\":\"paper_secs/secs_multimodal_kernel/Mirage Persistent Kernel A Compiler and Runtime for Mega-Kernelizing Tensor Programs/Acknowledgment.md\",\"basename\":\"Acknowledgment\",\"score\":6134.073146390668,\"foundWords\":[\"mirage\",\"mega-kernelizing\",\"persistent\",\"kernel\",\"kernelizing\",\"compiler\",\"runtime\",\"mega\"],\"matches\":[],\"excerpt\":\"# Acknowledgment\\nThis research is partially supported by NSF awards CNS-2211882 and CNS-2239351, a Sloan research fellowship, and research awards from Amazon, Cisco, Google, Meta, NVIDIA, Oracle, Qualcomm, and Samsung.\"},{\"filename\":\"paper_secs/secs_multimodal_kernel/KernelEvolve Scaling Agentic Kernel Coding for Heterogeneous AI Accelerators at Meta/KernelEvolve-Scaling-Agentic-Kernel-Coding-for-Heterogeneous-AI-Accel